          "system_name": "SUSE CVE Page",
          "text": "https://www.suse.com/security/cve/CVE-2026-4897"
        }
      ],
      "notes": [
        {
          "category": "general",
          "text": "A flaw was found in polkit. A local user can exploit this by providing a specially crafted, excessively long input to the `polkit-agent-helper-1` setuid binary via standard input (stdin). This unbounded input can lead to an out-of-memory (OOM) condition, resulting in a Denial of Service (DoS) for the system.",
          "title": "CVE description"
        }
      ],
